**curve.hpp defines validated, deterministic aim-response curves.**

## Interface

- `curve_kind`: `linear` or `power`.
- `to_string(curve_kind) noexcept -> const char*`.
- `response_curve`: `kind` defaults `linear`; `exponent` defaults `1.0f`.
- `validate(const response_curve&, string& why) noexcept -> bool`.
- `evaluate(const response_curve&, float t) noexcept -> float`.

## Contracts

`validate` requires finite exponent `> 0` for `power`; `evaluate` clamps `t` to `[0,1]`, preserving monotonic endpoints and output range, assuming validation.

## Dependencies

`types.hpp` supplies `string`; `utility.hpp` supplies curve-support utilities.